Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Port smolvla_expert_ref.py to LeRobot 0.7.0 / transformers >= 5.4

what:     frontend/smolvla_expert_ref.py (the host reference that writes the golden-reference keys):
          - make_att_2d_masks and create_sinusoidal_pos_embedding come from lerobot.policies.common.vla_utils;
          - the VLM forward runs with use_cache=True, past_key_values=None (no fill_kv_cache) and returns a DynamicCache;
          - the KV dump reads DynamicCache.layers[l].keys / .values ([1, 5, Lp, 64]), transposes to [Lp, 5, 64] and reshapes
            to [Lp, 320] (head-major columns);
          - phase `expert` rebuilds a DynamicCache from the npz with update(k, v, l) per layer (the reverse of the dump);
          - vision_position_ids takes the transformers 5 formula: idx * (1 / n) clamped to 1 - 1e-6, then bucketize
            right=True. The old `idx / n * (1 - 1e-6)` puts every row after the first one bucket lower (found in G2.1:
            the position ids differ from the ones SigLIP really uses);
          - docstring: environment line.
          Output keys and layout unchanged. build_policy (meta-device build) and materialise (buffer rebuild) needed no change.
why:      the crosscheck (G2.3) runs this reference in the same environment as infra/lerobot/golden_ref.py.
evidence: G2.2: run by file path in infra/lerobot/.venv (lerobot 0.7.0, transformers 5.22), cams 1, img-size 256:
          writes $SHVLA_DATA/golden/xc_ref.npz (132 arrays); vis_pos_ids equal to golden_ref.py's published.npz.
upstream: yes (the position-id formula bug is also worth reporting: with transformers 5, softhier-mlir's old formula
          gives different rows).
applies-to: softhier-mlir b11cd5fa4f3e717374d1e9ba14442ff302d1f970

---
